---
import ContentLayout from "@/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Dubai Battery Service"
  description="How Dubai Battery Service handles data: anonymous analytics, no forms, no data sold. WhatsApp and phone contact go directly to the service team."
  path="/privacy-policy/"
  crumbs={[
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Privacy policy", path: "/privacy-policy/" },
  ]}
  eyebrow="Legal"
  h1="Privacy Policy"
  lead="Short version: this site collects as little as possible, never sells data, and has no forms."
  heroCtas={false}
  sidebar={false}
  ctaBand={false}
>
  <p><em>Last updated: 24 September 2026</em></p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <p>
    {siteConfig.siteName} does not have sign-up or contact forms, and does not ask for your name, email or phone number on
    the website. We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how the site is used — for example which pages are visited and
    when someone taps a WhatsApp or call button. IP anonymisation is enabled, and the events we send contain no personal
    information: only the page, the service, the area and which button was tapped.
  </p>

  <h2>When you contact us on WhatsApp or by phone</h2>
  <p>
    WhatsApp and call buttons connect you directly to the independent mobile battery team that carries out the work. Any
    information you share in that conversation (such as your location or car details) is shared with them so they can
    help you, and is handled under their own practices and WhatsApp's terms. The pre-filled WhatsApp message contains no
    personal data.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Google Analytics sets first-party cookies to distinguish visits. You can block or delete cookies in your browser
    settings; the site works fully without them.
  </p>

  <h2>Data sharing</h2>
  <p>We do not sell or rent personal data. Analytics data is processed by Google under its terms.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy? Reach us through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</ContentLayout>
